From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:37:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Meshes: a run of faces with one texture drawn in one device
 call

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

With the vertices computed once (the previous commit), the meshes' largest
remaining cost on the handheld was handing each face to the device on its
own: every DrawGouraudPolygon chose a pipeline, looked the texture up in a
hash map (and checked it for a re-upload), found its descriptor set and
reserved vertex space -- the same answers for every face of a material.

- RenderDevice::DrawGouraudTriangles draws a run of triangles with one
  texture and one set of flags. Its default is one DrawGouraudPolygon per
  triangle, so the OpenGL and D3D11 devices are as they were; the texture's
  modified flag goes with the first triangle only, as the per-face calls
  had it.
- The Vulkan device does the set-up once and writes the same vertices and
  indices, in the same order, as that many polygons (the vertex writing is
  shared: WriteGouraudVertices). A run larger than the whole vertex buffer
  falls back to one triangle at a time.
- DrawLodMeshFaceDX collects consecutive faces with the same texture and
  flags and draws them when either changes, at the end, and before its
  out-of-bounds early returns, so every face is drawn in the order and at
  the point it was before.

Liberty Island under the Vulkan validation layer, with synchronization
validation, on both the bindless and the per-batch descriptor set path:
no messages.
